<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Euphrosyne of Polotsk</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">12th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Euphrosyne of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polotsk">Polotsk</a> was a princess of the Polotsk dynasty who became a nun and founded the Saviour Monastery at Polotsk, where she copied books and kept a school. She commissioned a jewelled reliquary cross, made by the master Lazar Bogsha in 1161 and lost in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>, and died on pilgrimage in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>. She is venerated as a patron saint of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belarus">Belarus</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/euphrosyne-of-polotsk.jpg" alt="Euphrosyne of Polotsk" width="320" height="642" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Нафонта Калашнікава · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:E%C5%ADfrasi%C5%84nia_Po%C5%82ackaja._%D0%AD%D1%9E%D1%84%D1%80%D0%B0%D1%81%D1%96%D0%BD%D1%8C%D0%BD%D1%8F_%D0%9F%D0%BE%D0%BB%D0%B0%D1%86%D0%BA%D0%B0%D1%8F_(1859).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
